> Module Ptc_family

> Using Types
> Using Params_2024 as P
> Using Rounding as R

# Premium tax credit, part 1: tax family size, poverty line, household income, applicable figure (Form 8962 lines 1 to 8)

Direct File ("DF" below) module `ptc.xml`
(`../direct-file/direct-file/backend/src/main/resources/tax/ptc.xml`, 9,760
lines), facts `/taxFamilySize` (line 1), `/ptcMagi` (line 2a),
`/householdIncome` (line 3), `/federalPovertyLevelThreshold` (line 4),
`/householdIncomeAsPercent` (line 5), `/applicableFigure` (line 7),
`/ptcAnnualContributionAmount` (line 8a) and `/ptcMontlyContributionAmount`
(line 8b). Issue #32, scope.md section 6.6. Law: 26 U.S.C. § 36B
(`sources/statute/irc-36B.html`), 26 CFR 1.36B-1 (`sources/regs/cfr-1.36B-1.xml`),
Form 8962 (2024) (`sources/forms-instructions/f8962--2024.pdf` p 1) and its
instructions (`sources/forms-instructions/i8962--2024.pdf`: Worksheet 1-1 and
Tables 1-1 to 1-3 p 8, Worksheet 2 p 9, Table 2 p 10, lines 8a and 8b p 11).
Tests are in `catala/tests/test_ptc_family.catala_en` (Table 2 in full in
`catala/tests/test_ptc_table2.catala_en`); the oracle comparison is
`difftest/mappings/ptc_family.mjs`.

## What this module computes, and how parts 2 and 3 plug in

- Output `ptc_annual_contribution_amount` (line 8a) and
  `ptc_monthly_contribution_amount` (line 8b, DF's `ptcMontlyContributionAmount`
  with its typo corrected) are the "contribution amount" that part 2 (#33)
  subtracts from the second lowest cost silver plan premium in Form 8962 line
  11(a) to (b) (annual path) or in each month of Part II line 24 (monthly path).
- Output `household_income_as_percent` (line 5) is what part 3 (#34) needs for
  the repayment limitation table (Form 8962 line 28 / Table 5) and for the
  "household income below 100 percent" tests. `household_income`, `tax_family_size`
  and `federal_poverty_level_threshold` are outputs too.
- All of it takes explicit scope inputs; the orchestrator wires them. The inputs
  and the module that supplies each (listed in the PR body) are: filing status
  (`Filers`), claimed dependents count (`Dependents.claimed_dependents_count`),
  the two "someone can claim" answers (`Filers`), the state (`Filers`), AGI
  (`Form1040.agi`), tax-exempt interest (`Interest`), nontaxable Social
  Security benefits (`SocialSecurity`).
- OUT OF SCOPE: Form 8962 line 2b (a dependent's modified AGI added to the
  household income when the dependent must file a return,
  IRC 36B(d)(2)(A)(ii)) and Form 2555 amounts (Worksheet 1-1 line 3). DF
  does not add them either and instead knocks the return out
  (`ptc.xml` `/dependentsRequiredToFile`, `flow.xml` line 100; foreign
  income is not supported). Part 3 or the return scope lists those knockouts.
- The inputs are complete (CONVENTIONS section 3).

## 26 U.S.C. § 36B(d) Terms relating to income and families

"(1) Family size. The family size involved with respect to any taxpayer shall
be equal to the number of individuals for whom the taxpayer is allowed a
deduction under section 151 (relating to allowance of deduction for personal
exemptions) for the taxable year."

"(2) Household income. (A) The term "household income" means, with respect to
any taxpayer, an amount equal to the sum of (i) the modified adjusted gross
income of the taxpayer, plus (ii) the aggregate modified adjusted gross
incomes of all other individuals who (I) were taken into account in
determining the taxpayer's family size under paragraph (1), and (II) were
required to file a return of tax imposed by section 1 for the taxable year.
(B) The term "modified adjusted gross income" means adjusted gross income
increased by (i) any amount excluded from gross income under section 911,
(ii) any amount of interest received or accrued by the taxpayer during the
taxable year which is exempt from tax, and (iii) an amount equal to the
portion of the taxpayer's social security benefits (as defined in section
86(d)) which is not included in gross income under section 86 for the taxable
year."

## Declarations

```catala-metadata
## Which poverty line table applies (Form 8962 line 4 check boxes).
## DF: ptc.xml /federalPovertyLocationOptions.
declaration enumeration FederalPovertyLocation:
  -- Alaska
  -- Hawaii
  -- Other

declaration scope PtcFamily:
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /filingStatus
  input filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  # DF: familyAndHousehold.xml /claimedDependentsCount
  input claimed_dependents_count content integer
  # DF: filers.xml /primarySomeoneCanClaimForTaxBenefits ("someone can claim
  # you as a dependent"). Filers output primary_some_one_can_claim_for_tax_benefits.
  input primary_someone_can_claim_for_tax_benefits condition
  # DF: filers.xml /secondarySomeoneCanClaimForTaxBenefits
  input secondary_someone_can_claim_for_tax_benefits condition
  # DF: filers.xml /livedInAk (state of residence is Alaska)
  input lived_in_ak condition
  # DF: filers.xml /livedInHi (Direct File does not offer Hawaii, so the
  # caller derives false from Types.ScopedState; the table is kept for the law)
  input lived_in_hi condition
  # Form 1040 line 11. DF: taxCalculations.xml /agi
  input agi content money
  # Form 1040 line 2a. DF: interest.xml /taxExemptInterest
  input tax_exempt_interest content money
  # Form 1040 line 6a minus 6b. DF: socialSecurity.xml /nonTaxableSocialSecurityBenefits
  input non_taxable_social_security_benefits content money

  # DF: ptc.xml /taxFamilySizeNegationBasedOnWhetherSomeoneCouldBeClaimed
  internal tax_family_size_negation content integer
  # Form 8962 line 1. DF: ptc.xml /taxFamilySize
  output tax_family_size content integer
  # DF: ptc.xml /taxFamilySizeIsZero
  output tax_family_size_is_zero condition
  # DF: ptc.xml /federalPovertyLocation
  output federal_poverty_location content FederalPovertyLocation
  # DF: ptc.xml /federalPovertyLineMagicNumberStartingNumber
  internal poverty_line_family_of_one content money
  # DF: ptc.xml /federalPovertyLineMagicNumberIncrement
  internal poverty_line_increment content money
  # Form 8962 line 4. DF: ptc.xml /federalPovertyLevelThreshold
  output federal_poverty_level_threshold content money
  # Form 8962 line 2a (Worksheet 1-1 line 5). DF: ptc.xml /ptcMagi
  output ptc_magi content money
  # Form 8962 line 3. DF: ptc.xml /householdIncome
  output household_income content money
  # Form 8962 line 5. DF: ptc.xml /householdIncomeAsPercent
  # (a decimal with a whole value: Catala 1.3 has no decimal to integer cast)
  output household_income_as_percent content decimal
  # Form 8962 line 7. DF: ptc.xml /applicableFigure
  output applicable_figure content decimal
  # Form 8962 line 8a. DF: ptc.xml /ptcAnnualContributionAmount
  output ptc_annual_contribution_amount content money
  # Form 8962 line 8b. DF: ptc.xml /ptcMontlyContributionAmount (sic)
  output ptc_monthly_contribution_amount content money
```

## Line 1: tax family size

Instructions for line 1 (`i8962--2024.pdf` p 7): the tax family is "you, your
spouse if you are filing a joint return, and your dependents. If you checked
the "Someone can claim you as a dependent" box, or if you are filing jointly
and you checked the "Someone can claim your spouse as a dependent" box on your
tax return, you or your spouse is not included in the tax family size
calculation for purposes of Form 8962, line 1." DF: 2 for a joint return, else
1, plus the claimed dependents, minus one for each filer someone can claim.

```catala
scope PtcFamily:
  definition tax_family_size_negation equals
    (if primary_someone_can_claim_for_tax_benefits then 1 else 0)
    + (if secondary_someone_can_claim_for_tax_benefits then 1 else 0)

  definition tax_family_size equals
    (match filing_status with pattern
       -- MarriedFilingJointly: 2
       -- Single: 1
       -- MarriedFilingSeparately: 1
       -- HeadOfHousehold: 1
       -- QualifyingSurvivingSpouse: 1)
    + claimed_dependents_count - tax_family_size_negation

  definition tax_family_size_is_zero equals tax_family_size = 0
```

## Line 4: federal poverty line

Instructions for line 4 (`i8962--2024.pdf` p 8): "Enter on line 4 the amount
from Table 1-1, 1-2, or 1-3 that represents the federal poverty line for your
state of residence for the family size you entered on line 1 of Form 8962.
(For 2024, the 2023 federal poverty lines are used for this purpose and are
shown below.)" The tables give $14,580 for one person in the 48 contiguous
states and DC, "$5,140 for each additional person" (family size 2 is $19,720,
8 is $50,560); Alaska $18,210 and $6,430; Hawaii $16,770 and $5,910. The
amounts of the tables equal the linear formula for every family size, which
`catala/tests/test_ptc_family.catala_en` checks against the printed rows.

```catala
scope PtcFamily:
  # DF checks Alaska first, then Hawaii, then the rest.
  definition federal_poverty_location equals
    if lived_in_ak then Alaska
    else (if lived_in_hi then Hawaii else Other)

  definition poverty_line_family_of_one equals
    match federal_poverty_location with pattern
    -- Alaska: P.ptc_poverty_line_family_of_one_alaska
    -- Hawaii: P.ptc_poverty_line_family_of_one_hawaii
    -- Other: P.ptc_poverty_line_family_of_one_other

  definition poverty_line_increment equals
    match federal_poverty_location with pattern
    -- Alaska: P.ptc_poverty_line_increment_alaska
    -- Hawaii: P.ptc_poverty_line_increment_hawaii
    -- Other: P.ptc_poverty_line_increment_other

  # A tax family of 0 (the filer is claimed as a dependent) has no line 4 in DF.
  definition federal_poverty_level_threshold equals
    if tax_family_size_is_zero then $0
    else poverty_line_family_of_one
         + poverty_line_increment * (decimal of (tax_family_size - 1))
```

## Lines 2a and 3: modified AGI and household income

Worksheet 1-1 (`i8962--2024.pdf` p 8): line 1 AGI (Form 1040 line 11), line 2
tax-exempt interest (line 2a), line 3 Form 2555 lines 45 and 50, line 4 "If
line 6a is more than line 6b, subtract line 6b from line 6a", line 5 the sum.
Line 3 of the form: "Add the amounts on lines 2a and 2b. Combine them even
if one or both of them are negative. If the total is less than zero, enter -0-
on line 3." Line 2b and Form 2555 are out of scope (see the top of the file).

```catala
scope PtcFamily:
  # DF returns $0 when the tax family size is 0.
  definition ptc_magi equals
    if tax_family_size_is_zero then $0
    else agi + tax_exempt_interest + non_taxable_social_security_benefits

  definition household_income equals Money.positive of ptc_magi
```

## Line 5: household income as a percentage of the poverty line

Worksheet 2 (`i8962--2024.pdf` p 9): "3. Multiply the amount on line 2 by 4.0. 4.
Is the amount on line 1 more than the amount on line 3? Yes. The amount on
line 1 above is more than 400% of the federal poverty line. Enter 401 here and
on line 5 of Form 8962. No. Divide the amount on line 1 above by the amount on
line 2 above. Do not round; instead, multiply this number by 100 (to express
it as a percentage) and then drop any numbers after the decimal point. For
example, for 0.9984, enter the result as 99; for 1.8565, enter the result as
185; and for 3.997, enter the result as 399."

DF rounds the household income and the poverty line to whole dollars before
dividing (both already are), truncates, and gives 0 for a tax family of 0.

```catala
scope PtcFamily:
  definition household_income_as_percent equals
    if tax_family_size_is_zero then 0.0
    else if household_income
            > federal_poverty_level_threshold
              * (decimal of P.ptc_poverty_percent_cap_multiple)
    then P.ptc_poverty_percent_over_cap
    else Decimal.truncate of
           ((R.round_dollar of household_income)
            / (R.round_dollar of federal_poverty_level_threshold) * 100.0)
```

## Line 7: applicable figure (Table 2)

"If the amount on line 5 is 150 or less, your applicable figure is 0.0000. If
the amount on line 5 is 400 or more, your applicable figure is 0.0850"
(`i8962--2024.pdf` p 10). From 151 to 300 the figure rises by 0.0004 per point
(151 is 0.0004, 200 is 0.0200, 300 is 0.0600). From 301 to 399 it rises by
0.00025 per point from 0.0600, rounded half up to four decimals (301 is
0.0603, 302 is 0.0605, 399 is 0.0848). DF reaches the half-up rounding by
adding 0.00005 when the unrounded value ends in 5 at the fifth decimal (an odd
number of points over 300). The full printed table is checked row by row in
`catala/tests/test_ptc_table2.catala_en`.

```catala
scope PtcFamily:
  definition applicable_figure equals
    if household_income_as_percent <= decimal of P.ptc_applicable_figure_zero_through
    then 0.0
    else if household_income_as_percent
            <= decimal of P.ptc_applicable_figure_linear_through
    then (household_income_as_percent
          - decimal of P.ptc_applicable_figure_zero_through)
         * P.ptc_applicable_figure_per_point_low
    else if household_income_as_percent <= decimal of P.ptc_applicable_figure_last_row
    then (round of
            ((P.ptc_applicable_figure_at_300
              + P.ptc_applicable_figure_per_point_high
                * (household_income_as_percent
                   - decimal of P.ptc_applicable_figure_linear_through))
             * 10000.0))
         / 10000.0
    else P.ptc_applicable_figure_max
```

## Lines 8a and 8b: contribution amount

"Line 8a. Multiply line 3 by line 7 and enter the result on line 8a, rounded
to the nearest whole dollar amount. Line 8b. Divide line 8a by 12.0 and enter
the result on line 8b, rounded to the nearest whole dollar amount."
(`i8962--2024.pdf` p 11.) DF truncates the product to cents before rounding
so that a product like $1,115.4958 is not rounded twice to $1,116; the
exact once-rounded product is the same value for a four-decimal figure
(`R.round_dollar_exact`). The line 3 amount is rounded to whole dollars first,
as DF does.

```catala
scope PtcFamily:
  definition ptc_annual_contribution_amount equals
    R.round_dollar_exact of (R.round_dollar of household_income), applicable_figure

  definition ptc_monthly_contribution_amount equals
    R.round_dollar_exact of ptc_annual_contribution_amount, (1.0 / 12.0)
```
